    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 no regressions and the three new/changed checkpoints (Cp01, Cp12, Cp44) are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to `POST /api/owners` (and the `PUT` update path) while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they appear on both request and response).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list \u2014 an owner may now supply its address via either form; validity is enforced in code.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner` entity: added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (`@Column`) with accessors.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four `schema.sql` files; converted the hsqldb `data.sql` seed inserts to explicit column lists so the new columns default to `NULL`.\n\n**Request handling**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (create): normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (trim/collapse/upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE). An owner is valid when it has a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address`, plus city. Structured fields win when present; the composed `address` is the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present. Falls back to the normalized flat address otherwise.\n- `ApplyOwner` (update): mirrors the same preference/composition logic.\n- MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps the new fields automatically by name, so the structured lines and composed `address` are stored and returned.\n\nSince city and postcode are shared across both address forms, the address-derived rules (household id via lastName+postcode, postcode validation, and locality) already read the structured input, and downstream storage/display now reads the composed structured `address`.",
